# publish = "." in netlify.toml means the repository root IS the web root, so
# anything committed here becomes a public URL the moment it deploys. A file
# ignored below is a file that cannot be published by accident.
#
# This list is a safety net, not a licence: it does not make a path private, it
# only stops the common accidents from ever being staged. Anything genuinely
# sensitive does not belong in this repository at all.

# Operating system clutter
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Dependencies. This project has no build step and no package.json, so a
# node_modules directory here would mean something went wrong. Ignored so that
# a stray npm install cannot publish thousands of files.
node_modules/

# Logs and crash output
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Environment and secrets. There are none in this project and there should never
# be: the site is static, it posts nothing, and it has no server to hold a key.
# Ignored anyway, because the cost of being wrong once is a published secret.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and IDE state
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local Netlify state, created by the CLI if anyone runs it here
.netlify/
